      "content": "You make a valid point, as uncontrolled borders and inadequate security measures can indeed lead to significant economic costs and social instability. Studies have shown that large-scale migration without adequate integration and control can result in increased healthcare costs, strain on education and labor markets, and housing and infrastructure pressures. Conversely, strengthened border security and enforcement can enable more efficient allocation of resources, mitigate potential disruptions, and maintain social order.",
